{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/96533-when-exactly-can-you-ask-cipher-key-questions","id":96533,"title":"When exactly can you ask Cipher Key questions?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-22T14:16:11-07:00","id":96533,"title":"When exactly can you ask Cipher Key questions?","content":"What exactly counts as a &quot;Beat in a scene involving angels, demons, stigmatics, or the God-Machine&quot; for the purposes of rolling for a Cipher Key question? Does it include:<br /> <br /> 1. The Beat gained from an Agenda Condition? The rules do say that it includes &quot;following&quot; your Agenda but make it subject to ST, where as an Agenda Condition Beat seems pretty objective. So it seems very slightly ambiguous.<br /> 2. The Beat gained from an exceptional success or a dramatic failure on a Compromise roll?<br /> 3. The Beats gained when guessing a wrong Cipher Key?<br /> 4. Any Cover Beat?<br /> 5. Beats gained as a Ring or in the presence of Ring members? As each demon is then in the presence of other demons. Or is the requirement to be in the presence of NPC demons?<br /> 6. Beats gained in a scene where angels/stigmatics are present but the players have not identified that that entity is an angel or a stigmatic?<br /> 7. Beats gained in scenes which take place in the vicinity of Infrastructure but not directly interacting with the Infrastructure<br /> <br /> My guess for 1 is &quot;yes&quot; and for 5-7 is &quot;no&quot; but it's not really 100% clear from the rules. 2-4 I don't really know; it could go either way. On the one hand they are personal to the Demon and do not result from any external interaction. On the other, they are directly related to the demonic nature.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2108-genesis","name":"genesis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T20:53:35-07:00","id":97264,"title":"","content":"Off the cuff:<br /> 1) Yes<br /> 2) Only if the exceptional success was on a mental or social roll directly involving angels/demons/stigmatics/God-Machine or the efforts thereof. (Punching them in the face doesn't bring you enlightenment, but sussing out how they've been manipulating the people around you can)<br /> 3) Potentially; failure can be as educational as success.<br /> 4) See #2. If the Cover Beat was gained by living the Cover or getting an exceptional success on a Compromise roll, either of which were in response to angels/demons/stigmatics/God-Machine or the efforts thereof, I'd allow the Demon to ruminate on what this means about their &quot;true&quot; place in the cosmos, and how they can achieve Hell.<br /> 5) I'd say no, unless it falls in one of the other ones here that say yes. Just being in the presence of other Unchained doesn't cut it for me.<br /> 6) and 7) No, unless the beat was about the efforts/incluences of the angels/stigmatics/Infrastructure <b>and the Demon knew the efforts/influences were God-Machine-relate</b><b>d.</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T03:57:37-07:00","id":97440,"title":"","content":"That's very helpful, thank you. Just to unwrap a couple of points as a bit more.<br /> <br /> On #2, I was talking about the beats you get on the Compromise roll itself, rather than the action leading to the compromise roll. The way I figured it, if you have a dramatic failure or an exceptional success on a compromise roll that teaches you something about you, the demonic you - either you get more skilled in manipulating reality and craft a piece of cover, defining yourself more, or you throw caution to the wind and get closer to your demonic form. Is your view that not every compromise roll would justify a Key question then? Bear in mind that a compromise roll itself would produce a beat only in exceptional circumstances.<br /> <br /> I suppose one can argue that a police investigation can cause a Compromise roll and that has nothing to do with the G-M but I suppose that's the core of my question: if the Cipher is about learning about your path to Hell and being a Demon rather than a Fallen Angel, does it necessarily have to involve external supernatural influence or can a demon do it by contemplating *its own* demonic condition. So say, a police investigation causes a compromise roll and the demon gets an exceptional success on it. Does that not teach the Demon something about a possible path to Hell? E.g. that they can turn weakness into strength by converting inconsistencies into stronger covers<br /> <br /> On #3. Rose Bailey said on rpg.net that she would also give a Beat for successfully guessing a Key. It would not be a part of the Cipher rules but rather the default ST discretion for major achievements. I wonder if that Beat could then be used to &quot;fuel&quot; a question about the next Key or whether it makes things too easy.<br /> <br /> On #4. What about a Cover Beat acquired from a pact? I'd say signing pacts is one of the most &quot;Demon&quot; and least &quot;Fallen Angel&quot; things that an Unchained can do","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2108-genesis","name":"genesis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T10:44:09-07:00","id":97604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>genesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/96533-when-exactly-can-you-ask-cipher-key-questions?p=97440#post97440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On #4. What about a Cover Beat acquired from a pact? I'd say signing pacts is one of the most &quot;Demon&quot; and least &quot;Fallen Angel&quot; things that an Unchained can do</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't <i>get</i> Cover Beats from pacts. You get Cover <i>Experiences</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T10:55:52-07:00","id":97609,"title":"","content":"Do you think that's a qualitative difference then? I was treating an Experience as 5 Beats and hence qualitatively the same","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2108-genesis","name":"genesis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T11:45:33-07:00","id":97641,"title":"","content":"Considering that the Cover Experiences received from pacts represent discrete connections that will presumably vanish with the loss of the Cover? Considering that the breadth of potential pactbound includes several things that aren't stigmatics which would only qualify for the roll if one drew the absurd conclusion that earning any Beat at all qualified the demon for the roll since it involved themself? Considering the point of the Cipher question criteria appears to be encouraging the risky behavior of associating with the entities whose involvement is required to allow the roll?<br /> <br /> Yeah, I think it's a qualitative difference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T04:18:54-07:00","id":98255,"title":"","content":"Uhm fair enough. That came across as somewhat more snarky than necessary, I think.<br /> <br /> You are explaining why a Pact should not trigger a Key question, which is fair enough. I thought you were suggesting there was a qualitative difference between Beats and Experiences generally. <br /> <br /> Anyway, what you appear to take as obvious (and which may well be correct) is precisely what I am unclear about from the text and what I am trying to ascertain in this thread.<br /> <br /> One way to interpret Cipher questions is how you have done; i.e. that it requires risky behavior with third parties. The other way (the way I originally read it but I am happy to concede that may have been incorrect) is that Cipher questions are rolled when a Demon achieves insight into its condition and its path to Hell. If it's the latter then there is no inherent necessity for risk or third party participation. For example, maybe you could assume demonic form and meditate, cashing in an Inspired Condition for a Beat.<br /> <br /> The first interpretation is certainly better gameplay and fits in with the horror genre more. But the second seemed, to me, more natural in the &quot;cosmology&quot; as described. Hence my uncertainty and questions. I appreciate I can ST how I want but was trying to establish the intended meaning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2108-genesis","name":"genesis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}